///   attached cell is only captured/new, re-materialize the trace continuation once
///   so the existing typed replay driver can reduce that late cell.
/// - Also stop extended retry_stop_drain once it sees a stable leaf with no queue and
///   no late captured cell left, avoiding another 256-pass no-op tail.
/// - No root completion, writer output, BuildOk, codegen, or value store success is
///   fabricated.
///
/// ALPHA511 REPLAY-DRIVER EXCEPTION FRONTIER:
/// - Alpha510 proved the payload path now hydrates and prefers the queued replay cell,
///   but the already-typed let_success_ready EApply now throws NullReferenceException
///   inside the reducer before replay_step/replay_reduce/replay_commit can be emitted.
/// - Do not leave that crashing task in the live queue for 254 identical retries.
///   When runReplayDriver throws, consume the offending task, preserve its payload/cell
///   on the frontier, and park as semantic_replay_driver_exception_blocked with a
///   dedicated receipt for the next alpha.
/// - Safety remains fail-closed: no Data/Ty/root completion/writer/codegen is fabricated;
///   the crash becomes a typed, resumable blocker instead of a hidden loop.

/// ALPHA510 REPLAY-CONTINUATION PAYLOAD PREFERENCE:
/// - Alpha509 proved the fingerprint-live-queue drain fires, but the queued task stays
///   at replay_id=1095/queue_depth=1 while the frontier remains
///   semantic_replay_fingerprint_repeat_blocked.
/// - runReplayDriver was choosing the current frontier semanticCell before trying the
///   queued replay_continuation payload.  For fingerprint-repeat frontiers this can
///   re-enter the stale blocked frame instead of the already queued typed child.
/// - Prefer the queued replay_continuation semantic_eval_payload over the repeat-blocked
///   frontier cell only in that narrow case, and emit an exception receipt if the typed
///   replay still fails before commit.
/// - Safety is unchanged: no Data, Ty, semantic_root_complete, writer output, BuildOk,
///   or codegen is fabricated; this only changes which already-recorded ReplayCell is
///   handed to the existing reducer.

/// ALPHA509 FINGERPRINT LIVE-QUEUE DRIVER DRAIN:
/// - Alpha508 proved that simply raising retry_stop_drain from 64 to 256 is now the
///   wrong move: the drain reached pass 255 with replay_queue=1 while the canonical
///   frontier was semantic_replay_fingerprint_repeat_blocked.
/// - The live queue contains an already typed term_replay_driver cell
///   (let_success_ready at testing.spi) but runBounded keeps re-reading the blocked
///   fingerprint frame and never invokes the queued driver.
/// - When retry_stop_drain sees a fingerprint-repeat frontier with a non-empty replay
///   queue, run the existing replay driver once, then re-peek before applying terminal
///   yield logic.  This mirrors the alpha505 leaf-complete queued replay drain, but
///   targets the repeat blocker exposed by alpha508.
/// - Safety is unchanged: no Data, Ty, semantic_root_complete, writer output, BuildOk,
///   or codegen is fabricated; only an already queued typed replay task is allowed to
///   run under the existing finite retry-stop bound.

/// ALPHA508 RETRY-STOP PROGRESSIVE LIVE QUEUE DRAIN:
/// - Alpha507 proved the longer terminal drain is not dead spinning: the live queue
///   extension marker fired from pass 12 through pass 63, replay ids advanced to 1071,
///   and the dynamic-record EApply leaf reached step 222 while replay_queue stayed 1.
/// - Keep the policy fail-closed but raise the retry_stop_drain live-queue ceiling
///   again, so the already queued typed replay can either discharge or expose a
///   genuine non-queue blocker beyond the current DRecord bridge loop.
/// - This does not fabricate Data, Ty, semantic_root_complete, writer output,
///   BuildOk, or codegen; it only gives existing replay tasks more bounded turns.
///
/// ALPHA507 LIVE QUEUED-REPLAY DRAIN EXTENSION:
/// - Alpha506 removed the DB dynamic-join blocker entirely and drove real replay through
///   DV@arg0/DV, DV@arg1/DV, TFun/TB child work, and dynamic-record bridge returns.
/// - The remaining retry stop is not a fresh missing writer/codegen proof: retry_stop_drain
///   keeps advancing a queued term_replay_driver behind a semantic_leaf_complete frontier,
///   but the fixed twelve-pass drain cap aborts with replay_queue still non-empty.
/// - Let retry_stop_drain continue longer, still bounded, when queued replay is live.
///   This only runs existing typed replay tasks; it does not fabricate Data, Ty, root
///   completion, writer output, BuildOk, or codegen.
///
/// /// ALPHA505 LEAF-COMPLETE QUEUED-REPLAY DRAIN:
/// - Alpha504 proved the ty/TFun<->TB artificial frame edge suppression works:
///   the new marker fires and TFun parent-continuation cycle count drops to zero.
/// - The new stop is a ty/TFun semantic_leaf_complete at spiral.spi:2670 with
///   replay_queue still non-empty; retry_stop_drain keeps asking for a missing
///   parent continuation instead of consuming the already queued replay tasks.
/// - During retry-stop drain only, if a semantic_leaf_complete frontier has queued
///   replay work, run the existing typed replay driver once and re-peek the
///   frontier before applying terminal-yield logic.
/// - This is scheduler-only and fail-closed: no value, Ty, root proof, writer
///   output, BuildOk, or codegen is fabricated.

/// ALPHA504 FRAME-SEMANTIC TY PINGPONG SUPPRESSION:
/// - Alpha503 got past the ready-duplicate replay suppression and drove the
///   let_success replay through apply/type-apply/deferred-ty children.
/// - The new blocker is a scheduler-invented frame_semantic_child ping-pong:
///   ty/TFun and ty/TB alternately install artificial parent continuations
///   until the parent-continuation cycle guard parks TFun->TB.
/// - Suppress only that artificial ty TFun<->TB frame-derived parent edge.
///   Real explicit parent continuations, stored TypeFun/TypeTerm spines, replay
///   drivers, values, writer gates, BuildOk, and codegen remain untouched.

/// ALPHA503 READY-DUPLICATE REPLAY RERUN:
/// - Alpha502 proved the leaf-yield LetSpine repair fires and reaches a real
///   let_success_ready replay envelope, but retry_stop_drain then repeatedly saw
///   the same driver_ready_replay_cell as a duplicate and refused to run it.
/// - For alpha502 leaf-yield terminal-let envelopes only, allow a capped rerun of
///   an already-ready duplicate replay task so the existing term replay driver can
///   consume the queued child instead of parking on duplicate=1.
/// - If the ready duplicate still repeats beyond the cap, park it as an explicit
///   semantic_replay_fingerprint_repeat_blocked frontier. No value, Ty, root proof,
///   writer output, BuildOk, or codegen is fabricated.

/// ALPHA502 LEAF-YIELD LET REPAIR:
/// - Alpha501 compiled and remained fail-closed, but its terminal ELet repair did not fire.
/// - Runtime showed retry_stop_drain first drained a ty semantic_leaf_complete frame; the
///   leaf-yield helper then selected the blocked term/ELet alternate and returned it
///   directly, bypassing tryYieldParentContinuationCycleBlocked.
/// - Repair that selected terminal ELet alternate in the leaf-yield path as well, by
///   rebuilding an existing LetSpine child replay envelope before the drain can stop.
/// - Still no fabricated values, writer opening, BuildOk synthesis, or codegen changes.
/// - Alpha500 proved the body->success escape path still fires, but the new
///   self-escape marker never appeared because the final ELet blocker is already
///   parked as a terminal retry-drain frontier, not re-entering continueToParent.
/// - When retry-drain sees a term/ELet semantic_parent_continuation_cycle_blocked
///   frame, inspect the stored LetSpine and rebuild a continuation envelope for an
///   existing missing body/success child before declaring the terminal blocker.
/// - This is fail-closed and capped per let/role/node: it schedules only nodes
///   already recorded in LetSpine and never fabricates Data, Ty, root completion,
///   writer output, or BuildOk.

/// ALPHA500 LET-SELF CYCLE ESCAPE:
/// - Alpha499 proved the let-body cycle escape is real: the runtime emitted
///   eval_worklist_parent_cycle_let_escape and scheduled let_success children.
/// - The new blocker is one level higher: the ELet frame itself can become the
///   child of a parent-continuation cycle after a scheduled success/body path,
///   leaving retry_stop with semantic_parent_continuation_cycle_blocked and no
///   queued replay.
/// - When a term/ELet child reaches the parent-continuation cycle threshold,
///   inspect its stored LetSpine directly and schedule any missing body/success
///   child before declaring the parent edge terminal.
/// - This stays fail-closed: it only queues an existing child replay from the
///   registered spine; it does not invent Data, Ty, root completion, writer
///   output, or BuildOk.

/// ALPHA499 LET-BODY CYCLE ESCAPE:
/// - Alpha498 proved the deferred-after-active-driver handoff works: the preserved
///   TFun child was scheduled after the parent driver unwound and resolved back
///   into the TPair parent.
/// - The next blocker is no longer TTerm/TFun retention; it is an EApply->ELet
///   parent-continuation cycle where the let body is already materialized by the
///   dynamic-record bridge but the same let_body edge keeps being replayed.
/// - When that exact cycle is detected, keep the cycle guard but redirect to the
///   next missing let body or the let_success child instead of parking on the
///   already-satisfied body edge.
/// - This is fail-closed: it only fires for term EApply children of term ELet
///   let_body_* continuations whose child term is already ready; it does not
///   fabricate Data, Ty, root completion, writer output, or BuildOk.

/// ALPHA498 DEFERRED REPLAY DRAIN:
    /// - Alpha497 proved deferred cells are now preserved, but the runtime stopped
    ///   with eval_worklist_deferred_replay_poke_suppressed/cross_kind_active_replay_driver:
    ///   the deferred child is safely queued, yet no handoff runs it after the active driver
    ///   unwinds.
    /// - Add a post-driver drain: when replayDriverActiveDepth returns to zero and the replay
    ///   queue is empty, materialize the next deferred cell as a normal typed replay task,
    ///   preferring ty/TFun and then term/EFun' families.
    /// - This is scheduler-only and fail-closed: the deferred cell still has to reduce through
    ///   the normal term/ty replay driver; no Ty/Data/root completion is fabricated.
    ///
    /// ALPHA497 DEFERRED TY-CHILD REPLAY:
    /// - Alpha496 proved the first concrete breakthrough: Sub/2 replay resolved as
    ///   semantic_root_complete and the build reached root_complete_handoff before moving
    ///   to a deeper TTerm conversion blocker.
    /// - The new blocker was not another pure op; it was a TTerm conversion repeatedly
    ///   discarding a same-kind deferred TFun child captured during active ty replay.
    /// - Preserve deferred replay cells and let a blocked TTerm schedule the deferred ty
    ///   child before reattempting conversion, instead of fingerprint-repeating the parent.
    /// - This remains fail-closed: no Ty/Data is fabricated, no root proof or BuildOk is
    ///   forged, and writer/codegen gates remain closed.
    ///
    /// ALPHA496 PURE SUB REPLAY:
/// - Alpha495 compiled and entered the replay driver; the runtime was interrupted
///   before retry_stop, but the live log exposed a concrete deterministic blocker:
///   term_op_args_available_unimplemented:Sub/2 on an EOp under base.spi:67.
/// - Add a conservative pure-op resolver for exact literal Sub and the x-0 identity,
///   mirroring the old evaluator's same-type literal subtraction without residual
///   codegen or writer/codegen gate changes.
/// - This is value-gated: missing args still schedule child work, symbolic Sub still
///   remains partial, and unsigned/signed behavior follows the existing literal cases.

#nowarn 40

// ALPHA980 REPLAY-OBLIGATION MODELING:
// - Runtime 979 did not fail with FS errors; it kept replaying and was interrupted manually while term/ty continuations still had queued replay obligations.
// - Alpha980 stops treating cross-kind/deferred replay as just a status string.  It introduces a ReplayObligation record carrying target, liveness, driver intent, repeat/cap and reason, then renders it only at the diagnostic boundary.
// - It also fixes an idle cross-kind starvation hole: if a queued replay exists but no replay driver is active, a cross-kind cell attachment wakes the driver instead of merely logging await_existing_replay_tick.
// - This is still a bridge, not the final pre-Hopac reimagining; the intended model is scheduler obligations over typed JoinPointKey/JPMethod/JPClosure evidence, not string status aliases.

// ALPHA979 TYPE-MODELING CORRECTION:
// - Alpha978 failed to compile because it used EvalWorklist-local SemanticStatusId constructors and the private semanticStatusToString renderer from an outer compiler scope.
// - Alpha979 fixes the scope error and stops treating the new DU as a dumb string alias in this branch: keyed global-fuse replay now builds a GlobalFuseReplayDecision carrying repeat/cap evidence, then renders status only at the DiagJson/Frame.status serialization boundary.
// - The original pre-Hopac compiler in i574n-spiral-main has no EvalWorklist/TermCycleFuse/SemanticStatusId layer; join points are modeled directly as JPMethod/JPClosure and codegen consults join_point_method/join_point_closure dictionaries. The real redesign target is to recover that typed shape under an explicit worklist, not keep growing string switches.

#if !INTERACTIVE
namespace Polyglot
#endif

module spiral_compiler =
    // Generic native-Hopac structural cutover scaffold. Version labels are external control; code names stay stable.
    type NativeCutoverTermKind =
        | NativeCutoverTermKind

    type NativeCutoverTyKind =
        | NativeCutoverTyKind

    [<Struct>]
    type NativeCutoverNodeId<'Kind> =
        | NativeCutoverNodeId of int64

    [<Struct>]
    type NativeCutoverReplayCursor =
        { cursor : int
          step : int }

    type NativeCutoverReplayShapeId =
        | NativeCutoverReplayApply
        | NativeCutoverReplayTypeApply
        | NativeCutoverReplayDeferredChild
        | NativeCutoverReplayParentContinuation
        | NativeCutoverReplayParentReplayCycleBreakPoison
        | NativeCutoverReplayStackFence
        | NativeCutoverReplayDynamicRecordBridge
        | NativeCutoverReplaySmallQueueParentPoison
        | NativeCutoverReplaySemanticStaleRetarget
        | NativeCutoverReplayIfUnknownReturnCondition
        | NativeCutoverReplayIdleCrossKindActiveTySidecar
        | NativeCutoverReplayOpImplRequired
        | NativeCutoverReplayUnknown of string

    type NativeCutoverReplayKey<'Kind> =
        { node : NativeCutoverNodeId<'Kind>
          shape : NativeCutoverReplayShapeId
          cursor : NativeCutoverReplayCursor
          site : string option
          raw_key_fallback : string option }

    type NativeCutoverMaterializedTerminalPayloadId =
        | NativeCutoverShadowTimeoutDeferredChild
        | NativeCutoverParentContinuationCycleShadowTimeout
        | NativeCutoverParentReplayCycleBreakPoisonTimeout
        | NativeCutoverStackFenceShadowTimeout
        | NativeCutoverDynamicRecordKeyBridgeTailTimeout
        | NativeCutoverSmallQueueParentReplayPoisonTimeout
        | NativeCutoverSemanticStaleRetargetTimeout
        | NativeCutoverIfUnknownReturnConditionTimeout
        | NativeCutoverIdleCrossKindActiveTySidecarTimeout
        | NativeCutoverOpImplRequiredHardSemanticBlocker
        | NativeCutoverQapVetoRejectedTerminal
        | NativeCutoverMissingLocalizedDriverAdapter

    type NativeCutoverHopacQuorumId =
        | NativeCutoverAltExpiredFailClosed
        | NativeCutoverIvarAwaitingFill
        | NativeCutoverMailboxProbeScheduled
        | NativeCutoverMailboxDispatchReady
        | NativeCutoverShadowOnlyBurnIn
        | NativeCutoverPrimaryEligibleButGated

    type NativeCutoverPendingGraphReadinessId =
        | NativeCutoverAwaitingChild
        | NativeCutoverAwaitingParentContinuation
        | NativeCutoverAwaitingCrossKindSibling
        | NativeCutoverTerminalPayloadMaterialized
        | NativeCutoverLocalizedDriverAdapterMissing
        | NativeCutoverReadyForPrimaryDispatchButGated

    type NativeCutoverQapVetoPolicyId =
        | NativeCutoverQapTelemetryOnly
        | NativeCutoverQapVetoRejectedByMaterializedTerminal
        | NativeCutoverQapVetoRejectedByHopacQuorum
        | NativeCutoverQapStillAllowedDuringShadowBurnIn

    type NativeCutoverRawKeyIdentityPolicyId =
        | NativeCutoverRawKeyForbiddenInAuthority
        | NativeCutoverRawKeyFallbackForDisplayOnly
        | NativeCutoverTypedReplayKeyDominates
        | NativeCutoverMissingTypedReplayKeyAdapter

    type NativeCutoverEvalWorklistShimPolicyId =
        | NativeCutoverEvalWorklistObserverOnly
        | NativeCutoverEvalWorklistCannotScheduleBackupTick
        | NativeCutoverEvalWorklistCannotOverrideTerminalPayload
        | NativeCutoverEvalWorklistDeletionBlockedByMissingDriverAdapter

    type NativeCutoverLocalizedDriverRouteId =
        | NativeCutoverRouteTermContinuationCell
        | NativeCutoverRouteParentReplayCycleBreakPoison
        | NativeCutoverRouteTyContinuationCell
        | NativeCutoverRouteStackFence
        | NativeCutoverRouteDynamicRecordBridge
        | NativeCutoverRouteDeferredChild
        | NativeCutoverRouteSemanticStaleRetarget
        | NativeCutoverRouteIfUnknownReturnCondition
        | NativeCutoverRouteIdleCrossKindContinuationCell
        | NativeCutoverRouteOpImplRequiredAuthoringSurface
        | NativeCutoverRouteMissingAdapter

    type NativeCutoverPendingGraphNode<'Kind> =
        { replay_key : NativeCutoverReplayKey<'Kind>
          readiness : NativeCutoverPendingGraphReadinessId
          terminal_payload : NativeCutoverMaterializedTerminalPayloadId option
          quorum : NativeCutoverHopacQuorumId
          children : NativeCutoverErasedPendingGraph list }
    and NativeCutoverErasedPendingGraph =
        | NativeCutoverTermPendingGraph of NativeCutoverPendingGraphNode<NativeCutoverTermKind>
        | NativeCutoverTyPendingGraph of NativeCutoverPendingGraphNode<NativeCutoverTyKind>

    type NativeCutoverFrontier =
        { name : string
          terminal_payload : NativeCutoverMaterializedTerminalPayloadId
          quorum : NativeCutoverHopacQuorumId
          qap_policy : NativeCutoverQapVetoPolicyId
          raw_key_policy : NativeCutoverRawKeyIdentityPolicyId
          eval_worklist_policy : NativeCutoverEvalWorklistShimPolicyId
          localized_route : NativeCutoverLocalizedDriverRouteId }

    type NativeCutoverPrimaryTransitionBatch =
        { stage : string
          frontiers : NativeCutoverFrontier list
          primary_hopac_still_gated : bool
          allows_compile_breaks : bool
          no_fabrication : bool }

    let nativeCutoverQuarantineQap terminal quorum =
        match terminal, quorum with
        | Some _, NativeCutoverAltExpiredFailClosed -> NativeCutoverQapVetoRejectedByMaterializedTerminal
        | Some _, NativeCutoverMailboxDispatchReady -> NativeCutoverQapVetoRejectedByHopacQuorum
        | None, NativeCutoverShadowOnlyBurnIn -> NativeCutoverQapStillAllowedDuringShadowBurnIn
        | _ -> NativeCutoverQapTelemetryOnly

    let nativeCutoverRawKeyPolicy typedKeyAvailable rawKeyPresent =
        match typedKeyAvailable, rawKeyPresent with
        | true, _ -> NativeCutoverTypedReplayKeyDominates
        | false, true -> NativeCutoverRawKeyFallbackForDisplayOnly
        | false, false -> NativeCutoverMissingTypedReplayKeyAdapter

    let nativeCutoverFrontier name payload route =
        { name = name
          terminal_payload = payload
          quorum = NativeCutoverAltExpiredFailClosed
          qap_policy = NativeCutoverQapVetoRejectedByMaterializedTerminal
          raw_key_policy = NativeCutoverTypedReplayKeyDominates
          eval_worklist_policy = NativeCutoverEvalWorklistCannotOverrideTerminalPayload
          localized_route = route }

    let nativeCutoverPrimaryTransitionBatch =
        { stage = "pending_graph_primary_transition_batch_shadow_gated"
          frontiers =
            [ nativeCutoverFrontier "deferred_child_cell" NativeCutoverShadowTimeoutDeferredChild NativeCutoverRouteDeferredChild
              nativeCutoverFrontier "parent_continuation_cycle" NativeCutoverParentContinuationCycleShadowTimeout NativeCutoverRouteTermContinuationCell
              nativeCutoverFrontier "parent_replay_cycle_break_poison" NativeCutoverParentReplayCycleBreakPoisonTimeout NativeCutoverRouteParentReplayCycleBreakPoison
              nativeCutoverFrontier "stack_fence" NativeCutoverStackFenceShadowTimeout NativeCutoverRouteStackFence
              nativeCutoverFrontier "dynamic_record_key_bridge" NativeCutoverDynamicRecordKeyBridgeTailTimeout NativeCutoverRouteDynamicRecordBridge
              nativeCutoverFrontier "small_queue_parent_replay_poison" NativeCutoverSmallQueueParentReplayPoisonTimeout NativeCutoverRouteTyContinuationCell
              nativeCutoverFrontier "semantic_stale_retarget" NativeCutoverSemanticStaleRetargetTimeout NativeCutoverRouteSemanticStaleRetarget
              nativeCutoverFrontier "if_unknown_return_condition" NativeCutoverIfUnknownReturnConditionTimeout NativeCutoverRouteIfUnknownReturnCondition
              nativeCutoverFrontier "idle_cross_kind_active_ty_sidecar" NativeCutoverIdleCrossKindActiveTySidecarTimeout NativeCutoverRouteIdleCrossKindContinuationCell
              nativeCutoverFrontier "op_impl_required" NativeCutoverOpImplRequiredHardSemanticBlocker NativeCutoverRouteOpImplRequiredAuthoringSurface ]
          primary_hopac_still_gated = true
          allows_compile_breaks = true
          no_fabrication = true }

    type NativeCutoverLegacyObserverActionId =
        | NativeCutoverObserverMayRecordOnly
        | NativeCutoverObserverBackupTickRejected
        | NativeCutoverObserverQapVetoRejected
        | NativeCutoverObserverMustYieldToPendingGraph
        | NativeCutoverObserverCompileBreakIfAuthorityRequested

    let nativeCutoverLegacyObserverActionText = function
        | NativeCutoverObserverMayRecordOnly -> "observer_may_record_only"
        | NativeCutoverObserverBackupTickRejected -> "observer_backup_tick_rejected"
        | NativeCutoverObserverQapVetoRejected -> "observer_qap_veto_rejected"
        | NativeCutoverObserverMustYieldToPendingGraph -> "observer_must_yield_to_pending_graph"
        | NativeCutoverObserverCompileBreakIfAuthorityRequested -> "observer_compile_break_if_authority_requested"

    type NativeCutoverPrimaryDispatchContract =
        { frontier : NativeCutoverFrontier
          graph : NativeCutoverErasedPendingGraph
          observer_action : NativeCutoverLegacyObserverActionId
          dispatch_before_backup_tick : bool
          physical_tail_is_authority : bool
          raw_key_allowed_for_authority : bool
          localized_adapter_required : NativeCutoverLocalizedDriverRouteId
          no_fabrication_boundary : string }

    type NativeCutoverRuntimeDispatchVerdictId =
        | NativeCutoverDispatchWaitForIvar
        | NativeCutoverDispatchPendingGraphBeforeLegacyTick
        | NativeCutoverDispatchTerminalCommittedFailClosed
        | NativeCutoverDispatchCompileBreakMissingAdapter

    let nativeCutoverRuntimeDispatchVerdictText = function
        | NativeCutoverDispatchWaitForIvar -> "dispatch_wait_for_ivar"
        | NativeCutoverDispatchPendingGraphBeforeLegacyTick -> "dispatch_pending_graph_before_legacy_tick"
        | NativeCutoverDispatchTerminalCommittedFailClosed -> "dispatch_terminal_committed_fail_closed"
        | NativeCutoverDispatchCompileBreakMissingAdapter -> "dispatch_compile_break_missing_adapter"

    type NativeCutoverLegacyTickGateId =
        | NativeCutoverLegacyTickAllowedWithoutTerminal
        | NativeCutoverLegacyTickSuppressedByPendingGraph
        | NativeCutoverLegacyTickSuppressedByTerminalPayload
        | NativeCutoverLegacyTickCompileBreakIfRequested

    let nativeCutoverLegacyTickGateText = function
        | NativeCutoverLegacyTickAllowedWithoutTerminal -> "legacy_tick_allowed_without_terminal"
        | NativeCutoverLegacyTickSuppressedByPendingGraph -> "legacy_tick_suppressed_by_pending_graph"
        | NativeCutoverLegacyTickSuppressedByTerminalPayload -> "legacy_tick_suppressed_by_terminal_payload"
        | NativeCutoverLegacyTickCompileBreakIfRequested -> "legacy_tick_compile_break_if_requested"

    type NativeCutoverHotRowRecyclePolicyId =
        | NativeCutoverHotRowEmitInitial
        | NativeCutoverHotRowEmitPeriodic
        | NativeCutoverHotRowSuppressAfterTerminalCommit

    let nativeCutoverHotRowRecyclePolicyText = function
        | NativeCutoverHotRowEmitInitial -> "emit_initial"
        | NativeCutoverHotRowEmitPeriodic -> "emit_periodic"
        | NativeCutoverHotRowSuppressAfterTerminalCommit -> "suppress_after_terminal_commit"

    let nativeCutoverRuntimeVerdictFor terminal quorum adapterReady =
        match terminal, quorum, adapterReady with
        | Some _, NativeCutoverAltExpiredFailClosed, true -> NativeCutoverDispatchTerminalCommittedFailClosed
        | Some _, NativeCutoverAltExpiredFailClosed, false -> NativeCutoverDispatchCompileBreakMissingAdapter
        | Some _, NativeCutoverMailboxDispatchReady, _ -> NativeCutoverDispatchPendingGraphBeforeLegacyTick
        | _ -> NativeCutoverDispatchWaitForIvar

    let nativeCutoverLegacyTickGateFor terminal quorum observerAction =
        match terminal, quorum, observerAction with
        | Some _, NativeCutoverAltExpiredFailClosed, NativeCutoverObserverCompileBreakIfAuthorityRequested -> NativeCutoverLegacyTickCompileBreakIfRequested
        | Some _, NativeCutoverAltExpiredFailClosed, _ -> NativeCutoverLegacyTickSuppressedByTerminalPayload
        | Some _, NativeCutoverMailboxDispatchReady, _ -> NativeCutoverLegacyTickSuppressedByPendingGraph
        | _ -> NativeCutoverLegacyTickAllowedWithoutTerminal

    let nativeCutoverBackupTickSuppressed terminal quorum observerAction =
        match nativeCutoverLegacyTickGateFor terminal quorum observerAction with
        | NativeCutoverLegacyTickSuppressedByPendingGraph
        | NativeCutoverLegacyTickSuppressedByTerminalPayload
        | NativeCutoverLegacyTickCompileBreakIfRequested -> true
        | NativeCutoverLegacyTickAllowedWithoutTerminal -> false

    let nativeCutoverHotRowPolicyFor committed seen =
        if committed && seen >= 8 then NativeCutoverHotRowSuppressAfterTerminalCommit
        elif seen < 8 then NativeCutoverHotRowEmitInitial
        elif seen % 128 = 0 then NativeCutoverHotRowEmitPeriodic
        else NativeCutoverHotRowSuppressAfterTerminalCommit

    type NativeCutoverLegacyLeakId =
        | NativeCutoverNoLegacyLeak
        | NativeCutoverLiveTailEvidenceRejectedAfterTerminal
        | NativeCutoverPinnedTerminalObserverRejectedAfterTerminal
        | NativeCutoverBackupTickRejectedAfterTerminal
        | NativeCutoverQapObserverRejectedAfterTerminal

    let nativeCutoverLegacyLeakText = function
        | NativeCutoverNoLegacyLeak -> "no_legacy_leak"
        | NativeCutoverLiveTailEvidenceRejectedAfterTerminal -> "live_tail_evidence_rejected_after_terminal"
        | NativeCutoverPinnedTerminalObserverRejectedAfterTerminal -> "pinned_terminal_observer_rejected_after_terminal"
        | NativeCutoverBackupTickRejectedAfterTerminal -> "backup_tick_rejected_after_terminal"
        | NativeCutoverQapObserverRejectedAfterTerminal -> "qap_observer_rejected_after_terminal"

    type NativeCutoverTerminalCommitClassId =
        | NativeCutoverNoTerminalCommit
        | NativeCutoverSingleFrontierTerminalCommit
        | NativeCutoverMultiFrontierTerminalCommit

    let nativeCutoverTerminalCommitClassText = function
        | NativeCutoverNoTerminalCommit -> "no_terminal_commit"
        | NativeCutoverSingleFrontierTerminalCommit -> "single_frontier_terminal_commit"
        | NativeCutoverMultiFrontierTerminalCommit -> "multi_frontier_terminal_commit"

    let nativeCutoverTerminalCommitClassFor committedFrontiers =
        if committedFrontiers <= 0 then NativeCutoverNoTerminalCommit
        elif committedFrontiers = 1 then NativeCutoverSingleFrontierTerminalCommit
        else NativeCutoverMultiFrontierTerminalCommit

    let nativeCutoverShapeForFrontier name payload =
        match name, payload with
        | "deferred_child_cell", _ -> NativeCutoverReplayDeferredChild
        | "parent_continuation_cycle", _ -> NativeCutoverReplayParentContinuation
        | "parent_replay_cycle_break_poison", _ -> NativeCutoverReplayParentReplayCycleBreakPoison
        | "stack_fence", _ -> NativeCutoverReplayStackFence
        | "dynamic_record_key_bridge", _ -> NativeCutoverReplayDynamicRecordBridge
        | "small_queue_parent_replay_poison", _ -> NativeCutoverReplaySmallQueueParentPoison
        | "semantic_stale_retarget", _ -> NativeCutoverReplaySemanticStaleRetarget
        | "if_unknown_return_condition", _ -> NativeCutoverReplayIfUnknownReturnCondition
        | "idle_cross_kind_active_ty_sidecar", _ -> NativeCutoverReplayIdleCrossKindActiveTySidecar
        | "op_impl_required", _ -> NativeCutoverReplayOpImplRequired
        | _, NativeCutoverSemanticStaleRetargetTimeout -> NativeCutoverReplaySemanticStaleRetarget
        | _, NativeCutoverIfUnknownReturnConditionTimeout -> NativeCutoverReplayIfUnknownReturnCondition
        | _, NativeCutoverIdleCrossKindActiveTySidecarTimeout -> NativeCutoverReplayIdleCrossKindActiveTySidecar
        | _, NativeCutoverOpImplRequiredHardSemanticBlocker -> NativeCutoverReplayOpImplRequired
        | _ -> NativeCutoverReplayUnknown name

    let nativeCutoverCursorZero =
        { cursor = 0
          step = 0 }

    let nativeCutoverTermReplayKey node shape site raw : NativeCutoverReplayKey<NativeCutoverTermKind> =
        { node = NativeCutoverNodeId node
          shape = shape
          cursor = nativeCutoverCursorZero
          site = Some site
          raw_key_fallback = raw }

    let nativeCutoverTyReplayKey node shape site raw : NativeCutoverReplayKey<NativeCutoverTyKind> =
        { node = NativeCutoverNodeId node
          shape = shape
          cursor = nativeCutoverCursorZero
          site = Some site
          raw_key_fallback = raw }

    let nativeCutoverTermGraph node shape site payload raw =
        NativeCutoverTermPendingGraph
            { replay_key = nativeCutoverTermReplayKey node shape site raw
              readiness = NativeCutoverTerminalPayloadMaterialized
              terminal_payload = Some payload
              quorum = NativeCutoverAltExpiredFailClosed
              children = [] }

    let nativeCutoverTyGraph node shape site payload raw =
        NativeCutoverTyPendingGraph
            { replay_key = nativeCutoverTyReplayKey node shape site raw
              readiness = NativeCutoverTerminalPayloadMaterialized
              terminal_payload = Some payload
              quorum = NativeCutoverAltExpiredFailClosed
              children = [] }

    let nativeCutoverGraphForFrontier (f: NativeCutoverFrontier) =
        let shape = nativeCutoverShapeForFrontier f.name f.terminal_payload
        match f.localized_route with
        | NativeCutoverRouteTyContinuationCell -> nativeCutoverTyGraph 63539353L shape f.name f.terminal_payload None
        | NativeCutoverRouteIdleCrossKindContinuationCell -> nativeCutoverTermGraph 48079639L shape f.name f.terminal_payload (Some "ty_to_term_or_parent")
        | NativeCutoverRouteOpImplRequiredAuthoringSurface -> nativeCutoverTermGraph 38208029L shape f.name f.terminal_payload (Some "term_op_impl_required")
        | _ -> nativeCutoverTermGraph 66594973L shape f.name f.terminal_payload None

    let nativeCutoverObserverActionFor (f: NativeCutoverFrontier) =
        match f.terminal_payload, f.quorum, f.eval_worklist_policy with
        | _, NativeCutoverAltExpiredFailClosed, NativeCutoverEvalWorklistCannotScheduleBackupTick -> NativeCutoverObserverBackupTickRejected
        | _, NativeCutoverAltExpiredFailClosed, NativeCutoverEvalWorklistCannotOverrideTerminalPayload -> NativeCutoverObserverMustYieldToPendingGraph
        | _, NativeCutoverMailboxDispatchReady, _ -> NativeCutoverObserverQapVetoRejected
        | _ -> NativeCutoverObserverMayRecordOnly

    let nativeCutoverPrimaryDispatchContractFor (f: NativeCutoverFrontier) =
        let observerAction = nativeCutoverObserverActionFor f
        { frontier = f
          graph = nativeCutoverGraphForFrontier f
          observer_action = observerAction
          dispatch_before_backup_tick = observerAction <> NativeCutoverObserverMayRecordOnly
          physical_tail_is_authority = false
          raw_key_allowed_for_authority = false
          localized_adapter_required = f.localized_route
          no_fabrication_boundary = "typed_pending_graph_payload_no_writer_no_root_no_buildok_primary_still_gated" }

    let nativeCutoverPrimaryDispatchContracts =
        nativeCutoverPrimaryTransitionBatch.frontiers
        |> List.map nativeCutoverPrimaryDispatchContractFor

    let nativeCutoverTerminalPayloadText = function
        | NativeCutoverShadowTimeoutDeferredChild -> "ShadowTimeoutDeferredChild"
        | NativeCutoverParentContinuationCycleShadowTimeout -> "ParentContinuationCycleShadowTimeout"
        | NativeCutoverParentReplayCycleBreakPoisonTimeout -> "ParentReplayCycleBreakPoisonShadowTimeoutPierce"
        | NativeCutoverStackFenceShadowTimeout -> "StackFenceShadowTimeout"
        | NativeCutoverDynamicRecordKeyBridgeTailTimeout -> "DynamicRecordKeyBridgeTailTimeout"
        | NativeCutoverSmallQueueParentReplayPoisonTimeout -> "SmallQueueParentReplayPoisonTimeout"
        | NativeCutoverSemanticStaleRetargetTimeout -> "SemanticStaleRetargetTimeout"
        | NativeCutoverIfUnknownReturnConditionTimeout -> "IfUnknownReturnConditionTimeout"
        | NativeCutoverIdleCrossKindActiveTySidecarTimeout -> "IdleCrossKindActiveTySidecarTimeout"
        | NativeCutoverOpImplRequiredHardSemanticBlocker -> "OpImplRequiredHardSemanticBlocker"
        | NativeCutoverQapVetoRejectedTerminal -> "QapVetoRejectedTerminal"
        | NativeCutoverMissingLocalizedDriverAdapter -> "MissingLocalizedDriverAdapter"

    let nativeCutoverQuorumText = function
        | NativeCutoverAltExpiredFailClosed -> "alt_expired_fail_closed"
        | NativeCutoverIvarAwaitingFill -> "ivar_awaiting_fill"
        | NativeCutoverMailboxProbeScheduled -> "mailbox_probe_scheduled"
        | NativeCutoverMailboxDispatchReady -> "mailbox_dispatch_ready"
        | NativeCutoverShadowOnlyBurnIn -> "shadow_only_burnin"
        | NativeCutoverPrimaryEligibleButGated -> "primary_eligible_but_gated"

    let nativeCutoverRouteText = function
        | NativeCutoverRouteTermContinuationCell -> "term_continuation_cell"
        | NativeCutoverRouteParentReplayCycleBreakPoison -> "parent_replay_cycle_break_poison"
        | NativeCutoverRouteTyContinuationCell -> "ty_continuation_cell"
        | NativeCutoverRouteStackFence -> "stack_fence"
        | NativeCutoverRouteDynamicRecordBridge -> "dynamic_record_bridge"
        | NativeCutoverRouteDeferredChild -> "deferred_child"
        | NativeCutoverRouteSemanticStaleRetarget -> "semantic_stale_retarget"
        | NativeCutoverRouteIfUnknownReturnCondition -> "if_unknown_return_condition"
        | NativeCutoverRouteIdleCrossKindContinuationCell -> "idle_cross_kind_continuation_cell"
        | NativeCutoverRouteOpImplRequiredAuthoringSurface -> "op_impl_required_authoring_surface"
        | NativeCutoverRouteMissingAdapter -> "missing_adapter"

    let nativeCutoverContractText (c: NativeCutoverPrimaryDispatchContract) =
        sprintf "frontier=%s|payload=%s|quorum=%s|observer=%s|before_backup_tick=%b|physical_tail_authority=%b|raw_key_authority=%b|route=%s|claim=%s"
            c.frontier.name
            (nativeCutoverTerminalPayloadText c.frontier.terminal_payload)
            (nativeCutoverQuorumText c.frontier.quorum)
            (nativeCutoverLegacyObserverActionText c.observer_action)
            c.dispatch_before_backup_tick
            c.physical_tail_is_authority
            c.raw_key_allowed_for_authority
            (nativeCutoverRouteText c.localized_adapter_required)
            c.no_fabrication_boundary

    let nativeCutoverPrimaryDispatchContractsSummary =
        nativeCutoverPrimaryDispatchContracts
        |> List.map nativeCutoverContractText
        |> String.concat " || "



    let nativeCutoverLegacyLeakPolicySummary =
        [ NativeCutoverLiveTailEvidenceRejectedAfterTerminal
          NativeCutoverPinnedTerminalObserverRejectedAfterTerminal
          NativeCutoverBackupTickRejectedAfterTerminal
          NativeCutoverQapObserverRejectedAfterTerminal ]
        |> List.map nativeCutoverLegacyLeakText
        |> String.concat "|"

    let nativeCutoverTerminalCommitSummary committedFrontiers =
        nativeCutoverTerminalCommitClassText (nativeCutoverTerminalCommitClassFor committedFrontiers)

    type RootCompleteHandoffBudgetId =
        | RootCompleteHandoffBudgetFastFail
        | RootCompleteHandoffBudgetLegacyWide

    let private rootCompleteHandoffBudgetText = function
        | RootCompleteHandoffBudgetFastFail -> "fast_fail_root_complete_handoff"
        | RootCompleteHandoffBudgetLegacyWide -> "legacy_wide_root_complete_handoff"

